export anchor Homepage1998Style:
    number: 160
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: 1998 homepage
    idea: A hand made 1998 personal homepage, with a tiled star background, centred bevelled tables, grey outset buttons, hazard striped under construction bars and the weekly numbers on green odometer hit counters.
    base: light
    palette:
        tile: #fff8dc, the tiled page background
        star: #c9dcff, tile stars with pink #f2d0e6, never text
        cell: #ffffff, table cells
        cream: #ffffe0, odd rows, list rows and system labels
        black: #000000, body text and counter cases
        linkBlue: #0000ee, links, with visited #551a8b
        navy: #000080, table heads and the logo
        teal: #008080, the greeting, column heads and last week bars
        magenta: #c000c0, this week bars
        maroon: #800000, the overdue alert, Behind and the tagline
        green: #006400, On track, with At risk in #8a4b00
        hazard: #ffd700, construction stripes with black and the note
        silver: #c0c0c0, buttons and the logo shadow
    type:
        The logo uses Times New Roman, Times, Liberation Serif, serif in
        bold italic 52px with a 3px silver drop, framed by tildes. The
        greeting uses Comic Sans MS, Comic Neue, Chalkboard SE, Trebuchet
        MS, sans-serif in bold 32px teal. Table heads, buttons and labels
        use Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif at 13 to 15px. Body uses Times New
        Roman at 15 to 16px with 1.35 line height. Counters use Courier
        New bold 22px.
    layout:
        One centred 800px column over a tiled star pattern. A black and
        yellow hazard stripe tops the page, then the italic logo, a maroon
        italic tagline, a row of grey outset nav buttons with Home pressed
        in and marked with a pointer, and a line holding the search label
        and inset field, Search, a yellow New project, Mail (4) and Signed
        in Mara Okafor. Grooved rules split every section. The welcome is
        centred, Welcome, Mara!! with the date and a double maroon box with
        diamonds for the overdue line. A bevelled table of four cells shows
        each number as a black odometer counter with green digits, the
        overdue counter in red, under a note that counters reset on
        Sunday. A bevelled projects table has a navy title row, teal
        column heads, cream striping, linked names, a striped blue
        progress strip, tasks, due and status. Two tables sit side by side,
        What's New? with red NEW! labels on the first items, and a bar
        chart built from table cells with values over each bar. A yellow
        under construction note and a second stripe close the page. Below
        640px the side by side tables stack, counters sit two by two and
        the projects table scrolls inside.
    spacing: Table cellspacing 2px and cellpadding 6 to 8px. Sections split by grooved rules with 16px around.
    density: Everything in one centred column, stacked like a long homepage.
    corners: All square.
    borders: 3px outset table frames, 1px inset cells, 3px outset buttons that turn inset when current, a double 3px box for the alert.
    shadows: None except the flat silver shadow on the logo. Bevels give depth.
    icons:
        Tiny solid glyphs. A tick means On track, a triangle with a bang
        means At risk, a cross means Behind, and a diamond with a bang
        marks overdue. Red NEW! labels flag fresh activity.
    focus: A 2px dotted black outline offset 2px.
    tone: Proud and excited with double exclamation marks, such as Welcome, Mara!!, What's New? and always under construction.
